course: dictionary
lesson: 9759
title: Words in business
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A supplier is a person or company that provides goods or services to other people or businesses, often regularly. Context helps you find this. «One car has parts from dozens of suppliers in different countries.» A car needs parts, and the parts come from suppliers, so a supplier must be someone who provides things.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Companies are pushed to check their suppliers.» Does "companies check the people or businesses that provide their goods" make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
explain: Suppliers can be different kinds of businesses. An energy supplier gives gas and electricity to homes, and a shop buys goods from a supplier to sell to customers. The word is the same, but the goods or services are different.
fact: A supplier is a person or company that provides goods or services.
fact: «Suppliers» is the plural of supplier, so it means more than one.
fact: A shop buys goods from a supplier and sells them to customers for more, which is how it makes a profit.
fact: Energy suppliers provide gas and electricity to homes.
fact: In 2021 a shortage of tiny computer chips stopped car factories around the world, because car parts come from many suppliers.
exercise: «One car has parts from dozens of suppliers in different countries.» What is a supplier? | A stranger who visits car factories | A customer who buys a car | *A person or company that provides goods or services to others | A type of car engine
exercise: Which of these is a supplier? | *An energy company that provides gas and electricity to homes | A teacher marking a test | A family eating dinner together | A child buying sweets at a shop
exercise: What is the plural of supplier? | *suppliers | supplying | supplyers | supplies
test: «In 2021 a shortage of tiny computer chips stopped car factories around the world.» Why did this happen to car factories? | Car factories stopped making cars because they were bored | *Car parts come from many suppliers, and the chips did not arrive | Computer chips are made from cars | Customers stopped buying cars
test: In a shop, what does the shop do with goods from a supplier? | *Buys them and sells them to customers for more | Gives them away for free to the supplier | Keeps them in a box and never sells them | Makes the supplier pay the customers
exam: «Phones need metals from mines in many countries; some mines have been unsafe or used child labour, so companies are pushed to check their suppliers.» Why do companies check their suppliers? | Metals are only found in one shop | Phones are too heavy to carry | *Some suppliers' mines may be unsafe or use child labour | Suppliers are always cheap, so companies like them
